# Graph Chat: organisation scope, parent chains and same-name catalogue items

Context: After the clean re-measurement, the remaining Graph Chat misses
came from scope rather than data. Totals for an organisation counted only
records booked directly by that unit (sub-branches were missing). "Parent
category" answers stopped one level up. Product rankings counted editions
that share a label under different ids separately, so a model sold under
two ids lost its top spot.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py (SYSTEM_PROMPT)
   Route H now separates people / organisations (same name = different
   entities, group by id) from catalogue items (same label = editions of
   one item, group by label and list the ids). New route I: organisation /
   category questions include all descendants by default (total* fields on
   pre-aggregated types, a descendant id set on fact records) unless the
   user asks for 직속 / 자체 / 직접. New route J: parent questions follow
   the parent link to the top and show the whole chain.
2. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py
   The route-order test expects 10 routes (A..J). A new test checks that
   the scope, parent-chain and same-name rules are in the prompt.

Modified files:
- src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
- tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" -p no:cacheprovider
--deselect tests/units/core/test_health.py::TestRunReadinessChecks
--ignore tests/units/api/test_routes.py`
-> 6053 passed, 2 failed (pre-existing test_deploy_instance_id cases from
the local deploy.config.sh), 316 skipped, 8 deselected.

# Graph Chat (LGE demo): absence check, state words, process tracing

Context: Prompt rules tuned on the LGE demo verification set. They stay on
the local LGE integration branch; the customer-neutral digest and link
fixes are in a separate commit.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py (SYSTEM_PROMPT)
   Check the digest / schema (including relationship and inverse fields)
   before saying a field, value or link does not exist; map state / kind
